    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327-a1">

                <pb facs="0655" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg531"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 168.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. D’Alton to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 23,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: My brother Joseph D’Alton, who is now
                    in a British prison, was born at Kenosha, Wis., December 12, 1850. I have sent
                    him the proofs of the same, which will be laid before our consul at Dublin,
                    Ireland.</p>
                <p>All he wants is a trial, as he can prove his innocence.</p>
                <p>Should you give this matter your attention, you will confer a favor on</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>AUSTIN L. D’ALTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>46 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Street</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Toledo, Ohio.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
